# Template. The real file lives only on the host at /opt/immich/.env
# (root:root, 0640) and is gitignored -- nothing in this repo deploys this one.
#
# One key, where upstream's .env has six. The other five -- UPLOAD_LOCATION,
# DB_DATA_LOCATION, IMMICH_VERSION, DB_USERNAME, DB_DATABASE_NAME -- are not
# secrets, they are the description of the deployment, and they now live in
# compose.yaml where a diff can show them changing.

# Password for the bundled Postgres. It never leaves the compose network: the
# database publishes no port, and the server and the database are the only two
# things that authenticate with it.
#
# Read at initdb time only. This host's cluster already exists, so editing this
# line does NOT rotate the password -- it gives you a server that cannot log in
# to its own database. ALTER USER inside the container is the way to rotate it,
# and the line here has to follow.
#
# THIS HOST IS ALREADY POPULATED: do not generate a new value. Copy the one out
# of /opt/immich-app/.env -- playbooks/immich.yml does exactly that for you on
# the first run, and only if /opt/immich/.env does not exist yet.
#
# For a restore onto an empty host, generate one with:
#   openssl rand -hex 32
#
# Hex on purpose. Immich's own template asks for A-Za-z0-9 only: the value ends
# up in a connection URL, where @ : / # ? % would need escaping to survive being
# parsed.
DB_PASSWORD=
